{"name":"Fat Tuesday","hex":"#352235","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fat Tuesday","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Tuesday before the onset of Lent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fat_Tuesday"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fat Tuesday (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Fat Tuesday was an American alternative rock band formed in Minneapolis, Minnesota in 1988. Initially founded by front man Andrew Crowley, the band comprised Crowley as a guitarist and vocalist, guitarist Michael Provence, bass guitarist Scott Kapp, and drummer Scott Anderson. The band's first album, So Much More, was popular in the Twin Cities in Minnesota and attracted the attention of record labels leading the band to be signed by Red Decibel Records and Columbia Records."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Fat_Tuesday_band_photo.jpeg/330px-Fat_Tuesday_band_photo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fat_Tuesday_(band)"},{"title":"Mardi Gras","blocks":[{"text":"Mardi Gras, also known as Shrove Tuesday, is the final day of Carnival ; it thus falls on the day before the beginning of Lent on Ash Wednesday. Mardi Gras is French for \"Fat Tuesday\", referring to it being the last day of consuming rich, fatty foods, most notably red meat, in preparation for the Christian fasting season of Lent, during which such foods are avoided."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/KosmicFrenchmenPurpleFaceMardiGras2009.JPG/330px-KosmicFrenchmenPurpleFaceMardiGras2009.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mardi_Gras"},{"title":"Fat","blocks":[{"text":"In nutrition, biology, and chemistry, fat usually means any ester of fatty acids, or a mixture of such compounds, most commonly those that occur in living beings or in food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Trimyristin-3D-vdW.png/330px-Trimyristin-3D-vdW.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fat"},{"title":"Tuesday","blocks":[{"text":"Tuesday is the day of the week between Monday and Wednesday. According to international standard ISO 8601, Monday is the first day of the week; thus, Tuesday is the second day of the week. According to many traditional calendars, however, Sunday is the first day of the week, so Tuesday is the third day of the week. In some Muslim countries, Saturday is the first day of the week and thus Tuesday is the fourth day of the week."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/IB_299_4to_Tyr.jpg/330px-IB_299_4to_Tyr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuesday"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/MardiGrasDakar.JPG/500px-MardiGrasDakar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/MardiGrasDakar.JPG/1280px-MardiGrasDakar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/MardiGrasDakar.JPG/500px-MardiGrasDakar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mardi Gras in Dakar, Senegal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMardiGrasDakar.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Marseille-carnival-sun-and-moon.jpg/500px-Marseille-carnival-sun-and-moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Marseille-carnival-sun-and-moon.jpg/1280px-Marseille-carnival-sun-and-moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi